                    {
                        "sense_id": "0de1d3e2-c7a5-344d-82fd-31d031b8ee99",
                        "entry_id": "babc7a9a-656a-3100-85ed-44fe1aa3bbbc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To wander in a wrong path; to stray; to go astray."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "407d2d3e-abd3-4e18-bfd3-9d8d2f3b359e",
                                "sense_id": "0de1d3e2-c7a5-344d-82fd-31d031b8ee99",
                                "text": "Her weary palfrey, closely as she might, Now well recover'd after long repast, In his proud furnitures she freshly dight, His late miswander'd ways now to remeasure right"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07c89a72-baf3-49f4-aaf3-5b69f764d1af",
                                "sense_id": "0de1d3e2-c7a5-344d-82fd-31d031b8ee99",
                                "text": "Or show you restless, miswandering, misclimbing ones new and easier footpaths?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efd96a82-2883-4a7e-846f-1c017b0d9414",
                                "sense_id": "0de1d3e2-c7a5-344d-82fd-31d031b8ee99",
                                "text": "The reason for this attitude toward Spain is not far to seek, and it finds an explanation in the words of José Ortega Gasset, quoted by Mr. Trend: Is it not bitter sarcasm that after and a half centuries of miswandering we are invited to follow the ...."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a8e842f-0d52-48c9-8b04-bef0dce7e304",
                                "sense_id": "0de1d3e2-c7a5-344d-82fd-31d031b8ee99",
                                "text": "As if it were a maze where these orphans of his heart had miswandered in their journey in life […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
